# f1 = add, f3 = low, f2 = turning, f4 = overVariables, f5 = overParameter, f6 = replacedInTheLoop, f7 = noTurn, f8 = attempt
# A bound function called in a loop that is built twice. The call asks the cell: a bound function . that many bound arguments . its target a closure of that function.
# A test that failed went to the call as written, which met the typed arm again: the result was anything, and the sum behind it went by the stub.
# In a turn that has done nothing, a test that fails begins the turn again in the closed copy of the loop: the result keeps the type that the copy of the target gives: the sum is one of whole numbers.
# Where the callee stands in front of the loop and every turn passes the call, the three tests are asked there and the words of the cell are read there: they never change behind its birth.
# RUN(SUMS): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# SUMS: = HasNumberOfBoundArguments
# SUMS: = Add {{*}}form=Integers
# RUN(HANDED): walk f5 mechanisms=all
# HANDED: = HasNumberOfBoundArguments
# HANDED: = Add {{*}}form=Integers
# The shell lays whatever it likes into the places: between two runs, and, called by the target itself, in the midst of a loop. A loop of no turn calls nothing, whatever stands there.
